  "commentary_text": "This is again a two-stage amplifier. A single-ended folded cascode is the first stage. The second stage consists of the two output transistors. Transistors M13/M15 and M16/ M18 form wideband level shifters between the output of the first stage and the Gates of the output transistors. They are bootstrapped out for AC signals. The quiescent current in the output transistors is set by two translinear loops. Output transistor M11 with M13 forms a translinear loop with transistors M23 and M21. Transistors M13 and M21 are equal and carry equal currents. The quiescent current in M11 is set by transistor M23. The same applies to the translinear loop of M12/M14 with M22/M20.",
